From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: prompt states keep and resume at any row

ai-engine f53c4ded2 transplanted onto the pin stack. The 2,048-row snap grid
goes: cuda_engine.chunkEnd cuts a chunk at its rows, the prompt's end or the
first mark past its start; prefillChunk takes its rows as a parameter (rank 0
chooses, the rows travel in the step's flags bits 16 and up, no rank re-derives
the cut); the family declares snap_min_rows (the admission floor) instead of
snap_grid and the generic snapshot rules drop planned/grid. GLM's prompt_pair
keeps the pin's pieces plumbing and gains drafterIdle (a pair allowed with a
drafter when both chunks end before the rows it ingests); the pin's
prompt_solo / prompt_pair choice stays as the `wide` step. shareSlot sits at
the capacity's own end. glm-resume-check: A fresh, B with a mark at R, C
resumed, equal bit for bit; a red control must differ.

Measurement (ai-engine docs/SPEEDUPS.md, f53c4ded2): next agent turn
1.31 -> 0.14 s at a 7.8k chat, 0.43 -> 0.15 s at 31k; two ABAB pairs.
Behaviour note: states now keep at marks and any chunk end, so a warm resume
lands on the reply's own rows instead of the last grid multiple.

Gates on pin+0001..0007: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host
green, whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new (era comment lines
single-lined to meet the rule).
